WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.601
SPEAKER:<i> He's just sort of part
 of the musical furniture</i>

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:03.636
of American culture.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:05.905
It's just wallpaper.

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:09.441
With Kenny G's music,
what can you say?

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:10.943
SPEAKER 2:
How're you feeling?

00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:13.079
Underappreciated in general.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.247
♪ (PLAYS SAXOPHONE) ♪

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.318
I don't think there's
anything wrong with hard work...

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.419
That's a hard lick.
I just played it really well.

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.321
<i> putting in the reps,
 and then reaping</i>

00:00:22.421 --> 00:00:24.757
<i> the reward of... "Hey,
 I'm really good at this."</i>

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:27.293
I think that's why my career
has lasted this long.

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:32.198
SPEAKER 3:
<i> The fact of the matter is,
 Kenny G, in the 1990s,</i>

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.500
was one of the most well-known
musicians on this planet.

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:36.869
KENNY G:<i> Somebody asked me,
 "What kind of music do you do?</i>

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.204
<i> Is it jazz?"
 I don't know.</i>

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.206
<i> You might think
 it might be jazz.</i>

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.874
"Well, is it pop?" I don't know.

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:42.942
You might think
it might be pop.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.111
SPEAKER 3:<i> He was having
 a huge impact</i>

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.912
<i> on defining what jazz is.</i>

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:50.149
<i> Even though the jazz community
 were looking at his music</i>

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:51.116
<i> with disdain.</i>

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:53.853
These are songs from my heart.
This is the way I just hear it.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.889
<i> They think I've just decided
 to play these kind of songs</i>

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.057
<i> because I knew
 they would sell well.</i>

00:00:58.157 --> 00:00:59.926
If only I was that smart.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.662
♪ (PLAYS SAXOPHONE) ♪

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:05.097
SPEAKER 4:<i> People have
 gotten married to his music,</i>

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:07.533
<i> had babies by his music.</i>

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.368
He makes playing an instrument
really cool.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.638
I been listening to him
since I was a baby.

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:15.374
At the same time, he is also
one of the most hated people

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:16.509
<i> in jazz.</i>

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.545
What the hell's not to like?

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.514
(AUDIENCE CHEERS)

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.250
SPEAKER:<i> There's something
 deeply powerful</i>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.753
about the fact that music
has reached millions of people.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.655
KENNY G:<i> The fact that
 what appeals to me</i>

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:32.826
also appeals to other people,
that's the beautiful thing.

